A1 — the noise floor, defined
====================================================================================
  Definition: sigma_floor = median over cells of SE(slope), where
  SE(slope) is propagated from the stored per-J standard errors by
  the delta method on the log-log regression. Previously the
  manuscript compared effects against 0.055 without saying what it was.

    boundary_raw.csv           n=144   median SE 0.0200   IQR [0.0160,0.0253]
    cliff_raw.csv              n=144   median SE 0.0214   IQR [0.0167,0.0305]
    control_raw.csv            n=72    median SE 0.0197   IQR [0.0155,0.0244]
    crossed_raw.csv            n=288   median SE 0.0217   IQR [0.0165,0.0273]
    ess_surface_raw.csv        n=36    median SE 0.0209   IQR [0.0183,0.0728]
    mechanism_raw.csv          n=144   median SE 0.0353   IQR [0.0246,0.0416]
    sigma_raw.csv              n=288   median SE 0.0219   IQR [0.0168,0.0273]
    visibility_raw.csv         n=144   median SE 0.0190   IQR [0.0125,0.0277]

    POOLED sigma_floor = 0.0219   IQR [0.0166,0.0291]   n=1260
    This is the number the manuscript should quote, with its IQR.

