====================================================================================
A3 — equivalence test, isotropic versus anisotropic at matched sigma
====================================================================================
  A gap below 0.05 is not evidence of equivalence. Two one-sided tests
  at the prespecified margin 0.05: equivalence holds only if the whole
  interval for the difference lies inside the margin.
  CAVEAT: the stored files hold cell means, not per-realization values,
  so the arms cannot be paired even though they shared seeds. This
  interval is therefore wider than a paired one would be, and the test
  is conservative.

