====================================================================================
A4 — where does degradation begin? change-point, not eyeball
====================================================================================
  Three models fitted to mean slope against log r:
    M0  single line;  M1  break fixed at the theoretical boundary r=1;
    M2  break at a free location, estimated by profile least squares.
  The manuscript may only say the empirical onset differs from r=1 if the
  interval for the free breakpoint excludes 1.

  diffusion        d     RSS M0     RSS M1     RSS M2      r_break    95% CI on r_break
  anisotropic     10     0.0419     0.0318     0.0076        2.000          [2.00,3.00]
  anisotropic     40     0.0147     0.0039     0.0015        1.500          [1.00,1.50]
  isotropic       10     0.0068     0.0042     0.0015        1.500          [1.25,3.00]
  isotropic       40     0.0705     0.0138     0.0109        1.100          [1.00,1.50]

  If the interval contains 1.0, the data do not distinguish the empirical
  onset from the theoretical boundary and the manuscript must say so.

